# Plan (sonnet, medium)

## Goal

While the opponent's board threatens lethal on the seat, `expand` in `crates/ai/src/search.rs` also keeps up to `AI_SEARCH.position_switches` switches of a unit to Defense Position that the width cut left out. Only switches that lower the threat count. The check runs on a clone with the unit's position set, so no search node is spent. Off lethal, nothing changes and the R1759000 tests pass unchanged. A new ruling, R2976000, amends R1759000. The requirements are an expansion test on the issue's example board, a puzzle that fails today, the R1759000 tests unchanged, and `cargo jackioh gate` at smoke size.

I ran the whole change in a scratch copy of `HEAD` outside the repo. Results:

- `cargo fmt --check` and `clippy -D warnings` are clean.
- `cargo test -p jackioh-ai --test ai` gives 774 passed.
- `--test ai_slow` gives 97 passed.
- `cargo test -p jackioh-server` passes (1700 + 670 + 202 and the smaller binaries, none failed).
- `cargo jackioh gate` at smoke size passes (20/20, 19/20 and 20/20 wins). A cold release build plus the run took about 6 minutes.

The numbers below come from that run.

## Files to touch

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `crates/ai/src/candidates.rs` | change: imports; new `pub fn wall_switches` right after `stands_down` |
| `crates/ai/src/search.rs` | change: import `wall_switches`; wire it into `expand`; doc comment of `expansion` |
| `crates/ai/src/config.rs` | change: doc comment of `AiSearch.position_switches` only; no value changes |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/search.rs` | change: new `mod wall_switches_2976` with 4 tests |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/puzzles.rs` | change: 1 puzzle in `mod tactics_b18` |
| `crates/ai/tests/ai/policy.rs` | change: `todays` mirrors the new rescue |
| `crates/ai/README.md` | change: one sentence in the move-order paragraph (~l.155-157) |
| `spec/rulings/R2976000.md` | new |
| `spec/rulings/R1759000.md` | change: title and one closing paragraph |
| `spec/pending/2976.md` | new: the §11 paragraph |

